hey what's up my name's samuel leeds i'm  30 years old i have a 20 million pound  net worth and i own a lot of properties  i own a castle and in this video i  wanted to answer the question i get  asked all the time which is how did i  get started how did i get started in  property aged 17 years old so if you're  interested in hearing my story then stay  listening and if you're thinking about  getting into property yourself maybe you  don't have a lot of money you're not  you're from a family of property  investors then maybe you'll get some in  interesting information and the golden  nuggets from this short video so the  first thing i want to say is when i  started out in property i just read a  few books inspirational motivational  books  from people like robert kiyosaki i read  a book called rich dad poor dad i read a  book called screw it let's do it by  richie branson and i remember reading  these books and i was i was just  finishing school  and i remember just thinking these guys  that are writing these books  they didn't do that well in school  which was for me a massive inspiration  because as i was finishing school and  i've just done my exams i was thinking  i'm not really cut out for this  academically  my exams i didn't do super well and i  wasn't particularly good in school so as  i was finishing school i was going down  the labouring type jobs i was doing a  bit of work for my dad i was working as  a plasterer i'd been just done some work  on a building site  all physical kind of jobs where you're  trading your time for money because i  thought going to university getting a  job working up the academic world that  really wasn't for me but what i realized  reading these books is there's a whole  third way  we always think in terms of at school  you can either use your hands and do  something practical or you can use your  brain and do something academic like be  a doctor or a lawyer or a builder  or an accountant or a driver  and what i realized is when i was a  teenager just as i was leaving school  reading these books is that there's a  whole third way and the third way is  being an entrepreneur the third way is  by being a business owner an  investor so i thought this is awesome  so i looked on google and i found some  property investment and business  meetings i found networking events  business networking international  property investors network i joined a  network marketing company called utility  warehouse and i signed up as a  distributor and i started going to these  business  entrepreneurial networks and it blew my  mind  and one of the things that really  surprised me was how a lot of people  took me seriously at school i was the  clown  in my family it was like oh you know  whereas now i'm at these business  networking events in a cheap suit and  people were like oh so what's your  strategy what people kind of believed in  me and took me seriously and i want to  give a big shout out as well to my  parents because my parents my mom my dad  and my stepdad you know although at  times  at times  my dad you know i had to leave the  family business and he wasn't  particularly happy about that when i was  like i want to be a property investor  but i want to give a shout out to my  parents and for the people in my family  who did believe in me i also want to  give a shout out to people at these  business networking events that actually  took me seriously even when i didn't  even take myself seriously because i  learned about property investment now  there's a big problem  this is where it's interesting so stay  listening  i didn't have any money  so even though i started learning about  business i had no money  so  i learned how to find property  investments but how can you be an  investor  when you don't have anything to invest  and one of the things the first really  important lesson that i learned  when i saw other people winning and i  started reading my books going to  seminars was that you don't have to have  money to invest yourself  to be a successful business owner or  property investor in fact most of the  people that are making a lot of money  even the banks  when the banks make money from property  investing they don't use their money  they use your money  and i thought all these rich people  they're tapping into other people's  money i can do the same  so just like how the banks use other  people's money to invest in property  that's crazy right the banks use your  money you save up your money and give it  to them and then they loan it out to  people at higher interest and they  invest in property and stocks crazy  that's what all rich people do so i  thought why can't i do that so my very  first property was in birmingham that i  found really good property i agreed to  buy for a hundred thousand pounds it was  worth 120. this was in 2009  and i borrowed  100 of the finance to buy this property  i got money from um from from the bank i  raised money  i couldn't get the mortgage because i  was too young and my stepdad tim  who i love for everyone ever and ever  agreed to basically be like a host of  this property and it was in trust for me  and i purchased this property using my  step dad's financial credit i used his  credit  and i used other people's and the bank's  money i found the property and i  purchased this when i was 17.  i then rented this property out room by  room  and lived off of the rent i'm like man  this is crazy um my second property that  i bought  i bought it on i got a 75  mortgage and i borrowed money off of an  investor for the deposit and i 100  i used other people's money i started  building a portfolio using other  people's money  i bought a property in 2010  on a buy now  pay later philosophy so this wasn't  borrowing someone else's money this was  stalling the payment but in the meantime  i'm getting the rent  so when i'm like 18 19 i'm getting all  this rent coming in i'm like man this is  nice because you don't have to actually  work to get rent but you just need the  property you rent it outside all this  rent coming in passive income  this is incredible and then the  properties in 2010 2011 after the crash  what happened they started booming the  values started shooting up when the  values went up  i'm making loads of money did i sell the  properties no i kept them i refinanced  them so i got a new more i borrowed  against them and i snowballed my  portfolio  and basically i'm now 30 and i'm in a  lot of debt  i've got millions of pounds worth of  debt but most high net worth individuals  are also high debt worth individuals so  although i've got a lot of debt i've  also got a lot of net and my passive  income is very high  and i make a lot of money  and that's how i got started in property  and where am i going now i guess now i'm  in development i'm buying pieces of land  i'm building houses from scratch and  i've also got this youtube channel to  help people get started in property  and i hope this video was helpful if it  was hit the like button drop a comment  below and i'll see you next time  [Music]
 

